Project scaffold + PDF viewer
Get a PDF rendering on screen with page controls
Step 1
Init project
Vite + React or plain HTML. Set up folder structure: /src, /assets, /components
Step 2
Install PDF.js
npm install pdfjs-dist. Load worker. Render first page onto a canvas element.
Step 3
Page navigation
Previous / Next buttons. Track currentPage state. Re-render on change.
Step 4
File upload UI
Drag-and-drop zone + file input. Read file as ArrayBuffer, pass to PDF.js.
MediaPipe hand tracking + gesture engine
Detect hands and map gestures to actions
Step 5
Webcam feed
getUserMedia() → hidden video element. Show webcam in corner preview box.
Step 6
MediaPipe setup
Install @mediapipe/hands. Run hand landmark detection on each video frame via requestAnimationFrame.
Step 7
Gesture classifier
Write classifyGesture(landmarks) function. Detect: fist, open palm, swipe, peace sign, thumbs up, pinch.
Step 8
Action dispatcher
Map each gesture to an action: swipe right → nextPage(), peace sign → toggleDrawMode(), etc.
Step 9
Debounce + cooldown
Add 800ms cooldown per gesture so one wave doesn't skip 5 slides.
Step 10
Confidence display
Show detected gesture name + confidence % in a small HUD overlay.
Annotation canvas layer
Draw, highlight, erase on top of the PDF
Step 11
Overlay canvas
Position a transparent canvas exactly over the PDF canvas using CSS absolute positioning.
Step 12
Pen mode
When draw mode is active, track fingertip (index finger tip landmark) and draw strokes on canvas.
Step 13
Highlighter mode
Switch context.globalAlpha to 0.35, stroke color to yellow. Same fingertip tracking.
Step 14
Color picker toolbar
Floating toolbar: red, blue, green, black, yellow. Click to switch active color.
Step 15
Shape tools
Gesture or button to switch to rectangle/circle/arrow mode. Track start + end fingertip positions.
Step 16
Undo / redo
Save canvas imageData snapshot after each stroke. Ctrl+Z or gesture pops the stack.
Step 17
Per-page annotations
Store annotations as JSON per page number. Restore when navigating back to a page.
Step 18
Clear page gesture
Flat hand sweep = clear all annotations on current page with a confirm flash.
Laser pointer + special tools
Laser dot, timer, thumbnail strip, pip camera
Step 19
Laser pointer
Thumbs up → show glowing red circle at index fingertip position. Animate with CSS pulse ring.
Step 20
Presentation timer
Floating countdown/stopwatch. Start/pause via gesture (3-finger hold). Color shifts red under 2 min.
Step 21
Thumbnail strip
Render all PDF pages as small canvases in a bottom scrollbar. Click to jump. Highlight current.
Step 22
Webcam PiP
Show webcam feed in draggable corner box using Picture-in-Picture API or canvas overlay.
Step 23
Snap to PNG
Gesture triggers html2canvas on the slide area → auto-download as slide-N.png
Step 24
Export annotated PDF
Use pdf-lib to embed canvas drawings as images on each PDF page. Download result.
Get the code for F4 ↗
UI polish + gesture cheat sheet
Make it look great for the demo
Step 25
Dark/light mode
CSS variable toggle. PDF canvas filter: invert(1) hue-rotate(180deg) for dark mode.
Step 26
Gesture cheat sheet
Press H or gesture → overlay modal showing all gesture icons + their actions.
Step 27
Toast notifications
Show "Next slide →", "Draw mode ON" toasts when gestures fire. Auto-dismiss in 1.5s.
Step 28
Fullscreen mode
F key or button → Fullscreen API. Gesture controls still work in fullscreen.
Get the code for F5 ↗
Express server + PDF upload
Set up Node.js backend with file handling
Step 1
Init Express app
npm init, install express, cors, dotenv, nodemon. Set up /api routes folder.
Step 2
Multer upload
POST /api/upload. Accept PDF files up to 20MB. Validate file type. Store in /uploads or Cloudinary.
Step 3
MongoDB connect
mongoose.connect(). Create File schema: name, url, uploadedBy, createdAt.
Step 4
File list API
GET /api/files → return all uploaded PDFs for logged-in user with URLs.
Get the code for B1 ↗
User auth (JWT)
Register, login, protect routes
Step 5
User model
Mongoose schema: email, passwordHash, createdAt. Add pre-save bcrypt hash hook.
Step 6
Register route
POST /api/auth/register → validate email, hash password, save user, return JWT.
Step 7
Login route
POST /api/auth/login → find user, bcrypt.compare(), sign JWT with 7d expiry.
Step 8
Auth middleware
verifyToken middleware. Attach req.user to all protected routes.
Get the code for B2 ↗
Annotation save/load API
Persist drawings per slide per user
Step 9
Annotation model
Schema: fileId, userId, pageNumber, strokes (JSON array), updatedAt.
Step 10
Save endpoint
POST /api/annotations → upsert by fileId + pageNumber + userId. Store strokes JSON.
Step 11
Load endpoint
GET /api/annotations/:fileId → return all pages' strokes for that PDF.
Step 12
Auto-save on frontend
Debounce 2s after last stroke → POST annotations to backend silently.
Get the code for B3 ↗
Real-time sharing with Socket.io
Let others watch your annotated presentation live
Step 13
Socket.io setup
Attach Socket.io to Express HTTP server. Create room per session ID.
Step 14
Emit slide events
On page change or stroke, emit to room: { type, pageNumber, stroke }.
Step 15
Viewer mode
Viewer joins room via share link. Receives events, mirrors presenter's slide and annotations.
Step 16
Share link generator
GET /api/sessions/share → create session doc with unique 6-char code. Return share URL.
Get the code for B4 ↗
AI features — slide summarizer + translator
The feature that puts you ahead of everyone
Step 17
Extract slide text
Use pdf-parse on the uploaded PDF. Extract text per page, store in MongoDB with file.
Step 18
Summarize endpoint
POST /api/ai/summarize → send slide text to Claude API. Return 3-bullet summary.
Step 19
Translate endpoint
POST /api/ai/translate → send text + target language to Claude API. Return translated text overlay.
Step 20
Frontend AI panel
Side drawer showing current slide summary. Language selector dropdown. Loads on gesture or button click.
